  ok   rule_ok equals relax_core.rule_ok
  ok   flag-off identity: inert_k with no open row == the exact rule (2,000 random blocks)
  ok   inert_k keeps whole rows whatever the argmax and goes on
  ok   inert_k stops at a mismatch on a row that is not open
  ok   inert_k: a rule row is kept only when its rule accepts the draft (rule C: p >= 0.1 p1)
  ok   comment: a row inside the comment is whole; the draft that ends the line and the row after it are exact
  ok   comment: the line-end guard (the 125B ends the line -> exact)
  ok   classify feeds a copy (the run's tagger is unchanged)
  ok   arms: D puts comments on rule C, C16 keeps them whole
  ok   comment: one that is or could become a tool comment ('# type:') is never open
  ok   comment: the fence's first two lines are never open
  ok   comment: a '#' inside a string is not one
  ok   only a fence that says python / py is open (a C fence's '#include' and an unlabeled fence are not)
  ok   docstring: a row inside is whole; a draft holding its quote character and the closing quotes are exact
  ok   docstring: not open while a run of its quote character is pending
  ok   docstring: the 125B closes it -> exact
  ok   arm C16 leaves docstrings exact
  ok   docstring: doctest lines stay exact, before and after the draft (R57_INERT_DOCTEST=0 lifts it)
  ok   a triple-quoted string that is data (assigned, returned, inside brackets, after a backslash, f-string) is never open
  ok   a docstring that is a statement of its own is open (raw prefix, module level, a method's)
  ok   guarded arm: lines 1-2 of a comment block and trailing comments whole, line 3 on the 125B's top-8
  ok   pre_block: rows in a span are sure in the cut; a 16-row arm leaves the block's length alone
  ok   pre_block at 32 rows: drafts past the 15th are kept only while they sit in a span (or are used copies)
  ok   copyrun_extend (BigMoE's CopyGate): a 31-copy block goes on to 63 drafts, its first 31 unchanged, no duel label past the drafter's picks; 32 rows or a broken run: unchanged
